A_{n+1} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} F_{n+1} & F_{n+2} \\ F_{n+3} & F_{n+4} \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} F_{n+2} & F_{n+1} + F_{n+2} \\ F_{n+4} & F_{n+3} + F_{n+4} \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} F_{n+2} & F_{n+3} \\ F_{n+4} & F_{n+5} \end{pmatrix} = A_{n+2}
\end{aligned}
$$
Hence
$$
D = |A_{n+1}| = \begin{vmatrix} 0 & 1 \\ 1 & 2 \end{vmatrix} \cdot \begin{vmatrix} 0 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 \end{vmatrix}^{n+1} = (0 \cdot 2 - 1 \cdot 1) \cdot (0 \cdot 1 - 1 \cdot 1)^{n+1} = (-1)^{n+2}
$$
and area $ABC = \frac{|D|}{2} = \frac{1}{2}$.

