Therefore, $\angle DJA = \angle DOA$, hence quadrilateral $ADJO$ is cyclic.
Since $AJ$ is the bisector of $\angle OAD$, the arcs $OJ$ and $JD$ are equal.
Hence $|OJ| = |JD|$.

Notice that $\angle TFB = \angle FDA$ because $FT$ is tangent to circle $BDF$, and moreover $\angle FDA = \angle CGA$ because quadrilateral $ADFG$ is cyclic. Similarly, $\angle TGB = \angle GEC$ because $GT$ is tangent to circle $CEG$, and $\angle GEC = \angle CFA$. Hence,
$$
\begin{equation*}
\angle TFB = \angle CGA \quad \text{and} \quad \angle TGB = \angle CFA. \tag{1}
\end{equation*}
$$
